# Young Poseidon: Repository Rules

## Scope and Sources of Truth
- This is a GameMaker/GML 2D platformer prototype, not a finished campaign.
- Inspect the relevant code, room instances, creation code and resource metadata before editing.
- Current code and room data take precedence over old design documents and completion notes.
- Read README.md for current state, FIXES_APPLIED.txt for implemented changes, and Що треба зробити.md for remaining work.
- Reference material is organized under Файли/Документація and Файли/Графіка; Файли/README.md indexes it.
- Files in Файли/Портфоліо are presentation material, not evidence of implemented functionality.
- Preserve the user's existing edits, especially manually placed room instances and tile layers.
- Keep changes scoped to the request. Do not refactor movement, AI, combat or save rules just to change graphics.

## GML and Events
- Follow existing modern GML functions, structs and bound methods; do not introduce abstractions without a need.
- Object Events live in separate GML files. Register added Events in the object's eventList.
- Register scripts in the project before referencing their functions.
- Keep player animation selection in the existing Create/Step/End Step/Animation End flow.
- Preserve spr_player as the player collision mask and keep feet/origin alignment consistent.
- Keep existing spriteMaskId values when replacing art unless changing collision is explicitly needed.
- image_xscale handles facing. Avoid combining a horizontal flip and 180-degree mask rotation unintentionally.
- One-shot actions and death must not loop; death must retain the existing checkpoint/respawn rules.
- Check is_dead and HP before interactions. Respect riding_cart and the existing pause lifecycle.
- Use yp_input, yp_key_name and yp_text/lc for rebindable actions and localized prompts; respect the hints setting.

## GameMaker Resources
- The current verified Windows runtime is 2026.0.0.23. Do not silently upgrade the project format.
- Clone a compatible resource from this project; never invent YY structure.
- Preserve resourceType, resourceVersion (currently "2.0"), schema markers, sequence/tracks and frame/layer references.
- YY/YYP files use GameMaker's JSON format, including trailing commas; use a compatible structured parser.
- Reuse existing resource names, frame GUIDs and folder entries where possible. Do not create duplicates.
- Register new resources in Young Poseidon.yyp and Young Poseidon.resource_order.
- Virtual folders are defined by the project Folders entries; verify parent paths against them.
- A sprite frame needs its composite PNG, layer PNG and matching sequence keyframe.
- Never reorder existing tile indices without migrating every affected room tile map.
- Tile graphics are not a substitute for obj_platform collision. Do not move collision geometry during an art-only edit.
- Preserve original PNG sources. Inspect actual sheet dimensions and frame/state boundaries before slicing.
- Update importer defaults, source manifests, validators and documentation if source files are moved.
- Import/build/place tools mutate resources. Do not run them as if they were read-only validators.

## Gameplay Contracts
- scr_save_system owns progression saves, permanent world state and automatic room routes; scr_settings owns persistent options.
- Keep progression files (`young_poseidon_autosave.ini`, `young_poseidon_save_1.ini` ... `young_poseidon_save_10.ini`, plus legacy `young_poseidon_save.ini`) separate from `young_poseidon_settings.ini`.
- Persistent world changes must use the world_state_* helpers. The default key is based on kind, room,
  object and authored xstart/ystart; set a unique world_state_id in Instance Creation Code when that identity
  could change or two authored instances would otherwise share a key.
- Mark permanent state before destroying or removing an instance. New games must call world_state_reset;
  loads must validate all data before replacing the active world state.
- Respect manually placed exits and blocks_auto_routes/blocks_auto_direction overrides.
- A placed boss is not proof of a complete arena or a verified playthrough.
- Boss victory and reward collection are separate explicit world-state records. Never infer a defeated boss only
  from an unlocked weapon/key; debug rewards must not silently complete fights.
- Do not change checkpoint coordinates, item-gated routes or save semantics as an unrelated fix.

## Verification and Reporting
- Use PowerShell 7 for tools. Run focused validators for the resources touched.
- Available validators: validate_player_animations.ps1, validate_enemy_sheets.ps1,
  validate_weapon_visuals.ps1, validate_level_tilesets.ps1, validate_interactive_props.ps1 (all in tools).
- Runtime tests: test_player_death.ps1, test_enemy_animations.ps1, test_weapon_visuals.ps1,
  test_menu_settings.ps1, test_interactive_props.ps1, test_world_state.ps1 (all in tools).
- Runtime tests build temporary copies with GameMaker; do not overwrite authored rooms with fixtures.
- After art changes, inspect a preview or Runner screenshot in addition to metadata checks.
- After room edits, verify actual instance placement and traversal; isolated tests do not prove the campaign is completable.
- If GameMaker is unavailable, report static checks only. Never claim a successful build/run without evidence.
- Keep README.md, FIXES_APPLIED.txt and Що треба зробити.md consistent: implemented work belongs in FIXES, remaining work in the backlog.
- Write user-facing documentation in Ukrainian, use accurate paths, and distinguish current checks from earlier test results.
